# Git shipping phrases

Remote is **`origin`** (`Bistro-Zur-Linde` only). Work on **`develop`**. Never push to `arrobabeto/bistro`.

## Actualiza cambios

`git fetch origin`. If there is local work, `git stash push -u` first. Merge latest GitHub (`origin/develop`, and `origin/main` into `develop` if main is ahead). Restore the stash. Do not commit, push, open a PR, or mutate Orbitype.

## Sube cambios

1. `git fetch origin` and compare `HEAD` to `origin/develop` and `origin/main`.
2. **If local is behind GitHub:** preserve local work (`git stash push -u` when the tree is dirty), merge remote commits into `develop` without `reset --hard` or discarding files, restore the stash, then **stop**. Do not commit, push, open a PR, or mutate Orbitype. Tell the user what was pulled, that their local edits were kept, and that they should say **Sube cambios** again when they have reviewed.
3. **If local is already up to date:** commit current work (if any), push `origin/develop`, open a PR to `main`, merge it, stay on `develop`.
4. **CMS sync (always after a successful GitHub merge in step 3):** run `pnpm run cms:sync-seed -- --yes --changed-only`. Saying **Sube cambios** is standing approval to upsert seed pages that differ from Orbitype (`INSERT` missing / `UPDATE` changed; skip identical). Report which pages were inserted, updated, or unchanged. Do not sync when step 2 stopped early. Seed is source of truth for pages defined in `seed-data.mjs` — keep CMS-only edits mirrored in seed before the next Sube cambios.
